<languages />
<translate>
<!--T:1-->
Your workflow calls the action once in each job, with <code>step</code> set to the job it runs in. The apply job's environment has the same name as the workspace.

<!--T:2-->
By default it applies after the merge, in HCP Terraform's order: a pull request only plans, and once it merges, the push to the default branch plans again and applies when the environment approves, or at once for a workspace in <code>auto-apply</code>. With <code>apply-before-merge</code> set to <code>"true"</code> on the <code>pending</code>, <code>apply</code> and <code>merge</code> steps, a pull request is applied first and merges once the apply succeeds.

<!--T:3-->
== Steps ==
{| class="wikitable"
! <code>step</code> !! Job !! What it does
|-
| <code>plan</code> || plan, before planning || Sets the <code>plan</code> output to <code>"false"</code> when a pull request changes nothing in the workspace's directory, the calling workflow or <code>shared-paths</code>, so the later steps can be skipped with <code>if: steps.&lt;id&gt;.outputs.plan == 'true'</code>. With <code>require-up-to-date</code>, refuses a pull request that is behind its base. Restores the providers dflook downloads, cached by the workspace's <code>.terraform.lock.hcl</code>, and saves them when the job ends.
|-
| <code>changes</code> || plan, after planning || Marks the workspace as having changes to apply.
|-
| <code>pending</code> || one job after the plans || Lists the workspaces to apply, and refuses an environment that is missing, or has no required reviewers unless its workspace is in <code>auto-apply</code>. Cancels older runs of the same branch that still wait for approval, unless one of their jobs is running. On a pull request it lists nothing, unless <code>apply-before-merge</code>, and then fails a pull request high in a [[Special:MyLanguage/Apply-before-merge#Stacked pull requests|stack]] that changes more than one workspace.
|-
| <code>apply</code> || apply, first step || Restores the providers the plan job cached, so the apply does not download them again. Records who approved, or that nobody had to. On a push, refuses unless the commit is still the head of the branch. On a pull request, refuses unless <code>apply-before-merge</code>, and then refuses when the pull request moved or merged, targets another branch outside a native stack, or with <code>require-up-to-date</code> fell behind.
|-
| <code>result</code> || apply, last step, with <code>if: always()</code> || Writes what the apply changed and whether it succeeded.
|-
| <code>gate</code> || the required check || Fails unless every job it needs succeeded. The apply job may be skipped.
|-
| <code>merge</code> || after the gate, with <code>apply-before-merge</code> || Merges the pull request through the async merge API, which also merges every pull request below it in a stack. When this run has nothing to apply, merges only if an earlier run of it was approved or applied an auto-apply workspace. Fails when the pull request has not merged 2 minutes after the apply, since production is then ahead of the default branch. Does nothing without <code>apply-before-merge</code>.
|-
| <code>collapse</code> || plan, last step, with <code>if: always()</code> || Hides, as outdated, every plan comment of <code>dflook/tofu-plan</code> or <code>dflook/terraform-plan</code> but the newest of each workspace. Comments starting with <code>**&lt;workspace&gt; apply: </code> are hidden the same way.
|-
| <code>log</code> || its own job after the apply jobs, with <code>needs</code> on them and <code>if: always()</code> || Comments the output of <code>log-step</code> in each <code>&lt;workspace&gt; apply</code> job on the pull request.
|}

<!--T:4-->
== Plan comments ==
The plan job's <code>dflook/tofu-plan</code> comments each workspace's plan on the pull request. Pushing again plans again, and the <code>collapse</code> step hides the older plan comments as outdated, so only the newest of each workspace stays open.

<!--T:5-->
The apply job should make a fresh plan and apply it only when it matches the approved one, as <code>dflook/tofu-apply</code> does without <code>plan_path</code> or <code>auto_approve</code>. On a push, dflook's plan updates the merged pull request's plan comment with the plan of the default branch, and the apply compares against that comment.

<!--T:10-->
== Apply logs ==
Run logs expire, so the <code>log</code> step keeps each apply's output as a comment on the pull request that it applied. After the merge, that is the pull request that merged the commit. The comment holds the output of the step that <code>uses</code> <code>log-step</code>, <code>dflook/tofu-apply</code> by default, without its folded groups, and only its end when it is too long for a comment. The <code>collapse</code> step hides the older ones.

<!--T:6-->
== Which commit applies ==
Only the newest commit of the default branch applies, since its plan carries the changes of every commit before it that has not been applied. So the push run has to plan every workspace that has changes, and the <code>plan</code> step's <code>plan</code> output is always <code>"true"</code> outside a pull request. A change made since the plan, such as a <code>workflow_dispatch</code> apply, makes the fresh plan differ and stops the apply; "Re-run all jobs" plans again. A commit pushed to the default branch without a pull request has no plan comment, so apply it with <code>workflow_dispatch</code>.

<!--T:7-->
== Job summaries ==
Each step writes a summary on the run page, so a reviewer can see what they are approving without opening the logs.

<!--T:8-->
{| class="wikitable"
! <code>step</code> !! Summary
|-
| <code>changes</code> || How many resources the plan adds, changes, destroys, moves and imports, the plan itself folded, and whether it waits for an approval.
|-
| <code>pending</code> || Each environment to apply and who can approve it.
|-
| <code>apply</code> || Who approved, or who started a run that needed no approval, and the commit it applies.
|-
| <code>result</code> || Whether the apply succeeded, with the same counts and plan as <code>changes</code>.
|-
| <code>gate</code> || Each job it needs and how it ended.
|-
| <code>merge</code> || Whether the pull request merged, and if not, why.
|}

<!--T:9-->
== Full workflow ==
This is the workflow of [[Special:MyLanguage/Get started|Get started]] with every step that runs after the merge. A <code>workflow_dispatch</code> run applies the chosen workspace from its branch once the environment approves, the <code>collapse</code> step hides outdated plan comments, and the job summaries show each plan folded.
</translate>

{{#tag:syntaxhighlight|<nowiki>
name: tofu
on:
  pull_request:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  workflow_dispatch:
    inputs:
      workspace:
        description: The workspace to apply from this branch, once its environment approves.
        required: true
        type: choice
        options: &workspaces [network, dns]
permissions: {}
jobs:
  plan:
    name: ${{ matrix.workspace }} plan
    if: github.event_name != 'workflow_dispatch'
    strategy:
      fail-fast: false
      matrix:
        workspace: *workspaces
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    permissions:
      contents: read
      pull-requests: write
    steps:
      - uses: femiwiki/terraform-github-tacos@v</nowiki>{{Version}}<nowiki>
        with:
          step: plan
          workspace: ${{ matrix.workspace }}

      - uses: actions/checkout@9c091bb21b7c1c1d1991bb908d89e4e9dddfe3e0  # v7.0.0
        with:
          persist-credentials: false

      - uses: dflook/tofu-plan@c7416238983bdd94c5486fb856bb7358f2bcc935  # v3.1.0
        id: plan
        env:
          GITHUB_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}
        with:
          path: ${{ matrix.workspace }}

      - uses: femiwiki/terraform-github-tacos@v</nowiki>{{Version}}<nowiki>
        with:
          step: changes
          workspace: ${{ matrix.workspace }}
          changes: ${{ steps.plan.outputs.changes }}
          plan-json: ${{ steps.plan.outputs.json_plan_path }}
          plan-text: ${{ steps.plan.outputs.text_plan_path }}

      - uses: femiwiki/terraform-github-tacos@v</nowiki>{{Version}}<nowiki>
        if: always()
        with:
          step: collapse

  pending:
    needs: plan
    if: </nowiki>><nowiki>-
      !cancelled() && (github.event_name == 'workflow_dispatch'
      || (github.event_name == 'push' && needs.plan.result == 'success'))
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    permissions:
      actions: write
      checks: read
    outputs:
      workspaces: ${{ steps.pending.outputs.workspaces }}
    steps:
      - uses: femiwiki/terraform-github-tacos@v</nowiki>{{Version}}<nowiki>
        id: pending
        with:
          step: pending
          workspaces: ${{ inputs.workspace && format('["{0}"]', inputs.workspace) || '' }}

  apply:
    name: ${{ matrix.workspace }} apply
    needs: pending
    if: </nowiki>><nowiki>-
      !cancelled() && needs.pending.result == 'success'
      && needs.pending.outputs.workspaces != '[]'
    strategy:
      fail-fast: false
      matrix:
        workspace: ${{ fromJSON(needs.pending.outputs.workspaces) }}
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    environment: ${{ matrix.workspace }}
    permissions:
      actions: read
      contents: read
      pull-requests: write
    steps:
      - uses: femiwiki/terraform-github-tacos@v</nowiki>{{Version}}<nowiki>
        id: approver
        with:
          step: apply
          workspace: ${{ matrix.workspace }}

      - uses: actions/checkout@9c091bb21b7c1c1d1991bb908d89e4e9dddfe3e0  # v7.0.0
        with:
          persist-credentials: false

      - uses: dflook/tofu-apply@e3e5dfc8f935d4b152c767801046f63abf8a77d3  # v3.1.0
        id: apply
        env:
          GITHUB_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}
        with:
          path: ${{ matrix.workspace }}
          auto_approve: ${{ github.event_name == 'workflow_dispatch' }}

      - uses: femiwiki/terraform-github-tacos@v</nowiki>{{Version}}<nowiki>
        if: always()
        with:
          step: result
          workspace: ${{ matrix.workspace }}
          outcome: ${{ steps.apply.outcome }}
          plan-json: ${{ steps.apply.outputs.json_plan_path }}
          plan-text: ${{ steps.apply.outputs.text_plan_path }}
          approver: ${{ steps.approver.outputs.approver }}

  # Make this the one required check
  gate:
    name: ${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' && 'tofu gate' || 'tofu gate (pull requests only)' }}
    needs: plan
    if: always() && github.event_name == 'pull_request'
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    permissions: {}
    steps:
      - uses: femiwiki/terraform-github-tacos@v</nowiki>{{Version}}<nowiki>
        with:
          step: gate
          needs: ${{ toJSON(needs) }}
</nowiki>|lang=yaml|copy=1}}

